{
  "id": "multivariable-calculus",
  "title": "Multivariable Calculus from First Principles",
  "summary": "A calculation-first and proof-aware bridge from single-variable calculus and linear algebra to geometry, optimization, and variational PDEs. Depth routes develop local and constrained Newton theory, inverse problems, weak formulations, nonlinear existence, compatible mixed elements, and elliptic boundary regularity.",
